<title>GERMANY: Buba says German Q3 GDP up 1.0 pct qtr/qtr.</title>
<headline>Buba says German Q3 GDP up 1.0 pct qtr/qtr.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-12-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bundesbank gave the following details of Q3 1996 GDP data:</p>
<p>PAN-GERMAN GDP   Q3 96    Q2 96	  Q1 96</p>
<p> qtr/qtr (pct)    +1.0     +1.5	   -0.5</p>
<p> yr/yr (pct)	+1.9     +1.1	   +0.3</p>
<p> GDP (bln dm)    772.0    765.8	  754.8</p>
<p>NOTE - Quarter-on-quarter figures are adjusted for inflation (1991 prices) and for seasonal and calendar factors. They are rounded to a half pct point. Yr/yr changes are calculated by Reuters based on Bundesbank data.  </p>
<p>WEST GERMAN GDP</p>
<p> qtr/qtr (pct)    +0.5     +1.0	   -0.0</p>
<p> yr/yr (pct)	+1.7     +0.9	   +0.4</p>
<p> GDP (bln dm)    698.8    693.7	  686.4</p>
<p>EAST GERMAN GDP</p>
<p> qtr/qtr (pct)    +1.5     +5.5	   -3.0</p>
<p> yr/yr (pct)	+3.8     +2.9	   -0.4</p>
<p> GDP (bln dm)     73.1     72.1	   68.4</p>
<p>NOTE - The figures are seasonally adjusted. The Statistics Office earlier gave the bulk of the third-quarter data based on unadjusted statistics.</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49-228-26097150</p>
</text>
